{"acceptedResponses":["A"],"answer":"A","bank":"amc","batch":"NA","choiceOrder":["A","B","C","D","E"],"choices":{"A":"\\(a\\gt9,\\) \\(b\\gt6\\)","B":"\\(a\\gt9,\\) \\(b\\lt6\\)","C":"\\(a\\gt9,\\) \\(b=6\\)","D":"\\(a\\gt9,\\) but we can put no bounds on \\(b\\)","E":"\\(2a=3b\\)"},"choicesType":"text","domain":[],"editorialNote":"","figureSources":{},"id":"1960_AMC_12_Q29","knowledgeGraph":{"assessedIds":["cnm_098"],"contentHash":"14164c7ca8d520c8dc0d43db3eaa38bd7cbfc185c762413aef1992c79dc109b4","flags":[],"reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"substitute-for-b","label":"Substitute for b","methodDirectNodeIds":{"substitute-for-b":["cnm_040","cnm_097"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_040","cnm_097"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"add-the-relations","label":"Add the given relations","methodDirectNodeIds":{"add-the-relations":["cnm_096","cnm_097"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_096","cnm_097"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_040","cnm_096"],"id":"eliminate-b","label":"Eliminate B's money","methodDirectNodeIds":{"eliminate-b":["cnm_098","cnm_097"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_098","cnm_097","cnm_040","cnm_096"]}],"status":"mapped","supportIds":["cnm_040","cnm_096"],"version":"1.0.0"},"level":"AMC 12","number":29,"question":"Five times \\(A\\)’s money added to \\(B\\)’s money is more than \\(\\$51.00.\\) Three times \\(A\\)’s money minus \\(B\\)’s money is \\(\\$21.00.\\) If \\(a\\) represents \\(A\\)’s money in dollars and \\(b\\) represents \\(B\\)’s money in dollars, then:","questionType":"text","rejectedAnswers":[],"responseType":"choice","schemaVersion":"3.0","skill":[],"solution":"The two statements translate to\n\\[\n5a+b>51,\n\\qquad 3a-b=21.\n\\]\nThe opposite signs of \\(b\\) suggest adding the relations to eliminate it. Since the second expression equals \\(21\\), this gives\n\\[\n(5a+b)+(3a-b)>51+21,\n\\]\nso \\(8a>72\\) and therefore \\(a>9\\). The equation then gives\n\\[\nb=3a-21>3\\cdot9-21=6.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\boxed{a>9\\text{ and }b>6}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).","solu